          "title": "Solving for an Unknown Given Two Perpendicular Vectors"
        },
        "question": {
          ":question/id": "9930d207-08cf-591b-868d-1ba033c13187",
          ":question/problem": "What is the value of $x$ given that $a=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3x\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $a\u22a5b$?",
          ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $a\u22a5b$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $a\\cdot b=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b &={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  &=3\\cdot x+4\\cdot 4+(-3x)\\cdot 3 \\\\  &=3x+16-9x \\\\  &=-6x+16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b &=0 \\\\ -6x+16 &=0 \\\\ x &=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
