        "question": {
          ":question/id": "a72b0aa0-023b-5f0c-83e6-f525bd7ca813",
          ":question/problem": "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3{r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3{r}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $g\u22a5h$ and $r>0$, find the value of $r.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $g\u22a5h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h &={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  &=(-2)\\cdot 2+3{r}^{2}\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 3{r}^{2} \\\\  &=-4-6r^{2}+9r^{2} \\\\  &=3{r}^{2}-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h &=0 \\\\ 3{r}^{2}-4 &=0 \\\\ 3{r}^{2} &=4 \\\\ {r}^{2} &=\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ r &=\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $r>0.$ Therefore, $r=\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
