          ":question/problem": "Let $u=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ a\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that $u\u22a5v$ and $a<0$, find the value of $a.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $u\u22a5v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v &={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y}+{u}_{z}\\cdot {v}_{z} \\\\  &=(-4)\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 3+a\\cdot a \\\\  &={a}^{2}-17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v &=0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-17 &=0 \\\\ {a}^{2} &=17 \\\\ a &=\\pm \\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $a<0.$ Therefore, $a=-\\sqrt{17}.$",
